WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.375
Why a Studio

00:00:01.199 --> 00:00:02.472
Display XDR hub

00:00:02.284 --> 00:00:02.779
cut

00:00:03.318 --> 00:00:04.544
A developer traced

00:00:04.356 --> 00:00:06.690
600 Mbps downloads

00:00:06.514 --> 00:00:08.813
on a 2.5 Gbps

00:00:08.625 --> 00:00:09.320
line to a

00:00:09.132 --> 00:00:10.877
USB Ethernet adapter

00:00:10.688 --> 00:00:11.490
plugged into his

00:00:11.302 --> 00:00:12.374
Studio Display

00:00:12.910 --> 00:00:14.018
Plugged straight into

00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:14.867
the MacBook Pro

00:00:14.997 --> 00:00:17.815
the Realtek RTL8156B

00:00:17.627 --> 00:00:18.935
adapter hit about

00:00:18.759 --> 00:00:20.704
2.3 Gbps

00:00:20.917 --> 00:00:21.907
behind the display

00:00:21.719 --> 00:00:22.721
it dropped frames

00:00:22.533 --> 00:00:25.162
above roughly 168,000

00:00:24.974 --> 00:00:26.270
frames per second

00:00:26.798 --> 00:00:27.623
The root cause

00:00:27.435 --> 00:00:28.165
he found

00:00:28.366 --> 00:00:29.486
the adapter sends

00:00:29.310 --> 00:00:30.571
only 4 USB

00:00:30.383 --> 00:00:31.526
packets per burst

00:00:31.574 --> 00:00:32.387
and the roughly

00:00:32.199 --> 00:00:34.486
7.6 microsecond go-ahead

00:00:34.298 --> 00:00:35.264
round trip through

00:00:35.076 --> 00:00:36.173
the monitor's hub

00:00:36.256 --> 00:00:37.210
makes the drain

00:00:37.022 --> 00:00:37.835
slower than the

00:00:37.647 --> 00:00:40.017
2.5 Gbps input

00:00:40.542 --> 00:00:41.556
Full story on

00:00:41.367 --> 00:00:42.263
the dashboard
